# {{projectName}}

Generated by `create-prisma` with the Astro template.

## Scripts

- `{{runScriptCommand packageManager "dev"}}` - start the Astro dev server
- `{{runScriptCommand packageManager "build"}}` - build for production
- `{{runScriptCommand packageManager "preview"}}` - preview the production build
- `{{runScriptCommand packageManager "astro"}}` - run Astro CLI commands
- `{{runScriptCommand packageManager "deploy"}}` - build and deploy with Prisma Composer

## Prisma

Prisma setup is scaffolded automatically in:

- `prisma/schema.prisma`
- `prisma/seed.ts`
- `src/lib/prisma.ts`
- `src/pages/api/users.ts`
- `prisma.config.ts`
- `module.ts`
- `service.ts`
- `prisma-composer.config.ts`
- `src/generated/prisma`

Database helper scripts are added to `package.json`:

- `db:generate`
- `db:push`
- `db:migrate`
- `db:seed`

The starter page queries a basic `User` model in `src/pages/index.astro`, and `src/pages/api/users.ts` shows an Astro API route backed by the same Prisma client.

## Prisma Composer

The application topology is declared in `module.ts` and `service.ts`, with deploy configuration in `prisma-composer.config.ts`. {{#if composerPostgres}}Composer provisions Prisma Postgres and injects its connection into the service.{{else}}The database URL is bound as a secret service input from `.env`.{{/if}}

Run `{{runScriptCommand packageManager "deploy"}}` to deploy later changes.
